## ChkTeX policy for `just latex::lint`. Correctness (unresolved references,
## citations and glyphs) is gated by tools/check-log and the compile itself;
## ChkTeX is style. Suppressed classes fire falsely on math-heavy prose:
## 1 (command terminated with space), 2 (nbsp before inline math), 3 (enclose
## braces), 8 (dash length), 12/13 (interword and intersentence spacing),
## 24 (space before \label), 26 (space before punctuation), 35/36/38
## (math and quote heuristics) and 46 (use \( \) instead of $ $).
CmdLine
{
    -n1 -n2 -n3 -n8 -n12 -n13 -n24 -n26 -n35 -n36 -n38 -n46
}
